      "title": "Heartbeat RPC latency p95",
      "description": "How long the heartbeat call itself takes. Matters because the throttle interval is a floor on the SEND rate, not a budget for the round trip -- a slow heartbeat RPC eats into the 20% margin between the throttle and the timeout. Shares the temporal_request_latency bucket override.",
